# Line endings, and why this file is the first fix in the repository.
#
# Everything under kindle/ ends up on a Kindle 4, where the shell is busybox
# `ash`. That shell does not treat a carriage return as whitespace: it is an
# ordinary character, part of whatever token it happens to end. A checkout that
# turned LF into CRLF therefore ships scripts in which
#
#     DASH_DIR=${DASH_DIR:-/mnt/us/dashboard}
#
# assigns "/mnt/us/dashboard\r" — a directory that does not exist — and
#
#     export INTERACT=${INTERACT:-true}
#
# assigns "true\r", which is not equal to "true", so every feature guarded by
# that comparison silently turns itself off. Both failures are invisible on a
# device with no terminal: the panel simply does not start, and the page
# buttons simply do nothing.
#
# Git for Windows enables core.autocrlf=true by default, so a clone on Windows
# does exactly that unless it is told otherwise. This file tells it otherwise,
# for every contributor and on every platform, and it overrides core.autocrlf.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf`: normalise to LF in the repository AND check out LF in the
# working tree. Not `text=auto` alone — that would still hand Windows a CRLF
# working tree, which is the half that reaches the Kindle.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Named explicitly rather than left to the auto-detection: these are the files
# whose line endings are load-bearing, and "auto" is a guess about content.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.xml     text eol=lf
*.j2      text eol=lf
*.css     text eol=lf
*.svg     text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
LICENSE   text eol=lf

# The one exception. PowerShell is the Windows-side entry point and is never
# copied to the Kindle; some PowerShell hosts still dislike bare LF.
*.ps1     text eol=crlf

# Binary, so Git never touches them. Without these, `text=auto` guessing wrong
# about a PNG or a font would corrupt it on checkout.
*.png     binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ico     binary
*.jpg     binary
